@@ -0,0 +1,161 @@
+# Larch repository migration
+
+This adaptation migrates `character-ai/larch` into the existing public
+`zhupanov/larch` fork. It is based on NicholasBoll/github-migration commit
+`241c203953fb516609b16f454098daa1b48d7d73`. The source repository is read-only.
+The destination's original planning issues and Git refs are preserved.
+
+Run this operator tool outside the larch plugin checkout. Use Node 24, Git,
+GitHub CLI, and `npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund`. Credentials come
+from the authenticated `gh` login or the `MIGRATION_SOURCE_TOKEN` and
+`MIGRATION_TARGET_TOKEN` environment variables. Keep credential values out of
+commands, patches, logs, and archives. If an old `GH_TOKEN` or `GITHUB_TOKEN`
+overrides a refreshed stored login, unset that override before running a stage.
+
+The parent operator directory holds `baseline/`, `reports/`,
+`baseline-release/`, and an immutable copy of the source export. The working
+`larch/` directory contains the export, per-object state, audit ledger, history
+supplement, and research archive. Keep these owner-held files private. GitHub
+responses can include historical context from other repositories accessible to
+the operator. Commit the tool and sanitized inventories; retain raw data in
+private storage.
+
+## Historical import
+
+Suppress destination Actions and other import-triggered integrations first.
+Every historical stage verifies that Actions remains disabled. The operator
+confirmed no destination GitHub Apps; inventories found no webhooks and
+disabled Dependabot updates. The write adapter spaces requests at 400 per hour,
+honors GitHub rate-limit headers, prohibits source writes, and stops on errors.
+
+The validated order is:
+
+1. Preserve `fetch` outputs and their checksums, plus a complete source Git mirror.
+2. Run `rewriteRefs`, inspect its three no-diff archival exceptions, then run
+   `createBranches` and `node provisionMetadata.js` with `MIGRATION_WRITE=1`.
+3. Run `createIssues`, `createComments`, and `updateIssues` in that order.
+   Run `auditReplay`, retain and download-verify its private backup, then
+   complete leaf 4 through `node completeHistoricalLeaf.js 4`.
+4. Complete `node fetchHistory.js` and `node fetchLinkedIssues.js`. These are
+   read-only source collectors and can run while destination import proceeds.
+5. Run `repairHistoryReferences`, `restoreNativeRelations`,
+   `buildHistoryArchive`, and `auditHistorical` in that order.
+6. Run `deleteBranches`, then verify the historical archive and remote PRs
+   again. Retain a checksummed private backup and download it to verify its bytes.
+   Complete leaf 5 through `node completeHistoricalLeaf.js 5`.
+
+Stage names above are npm scripts unless a `node` command is shown. Historical
+write stages require `MIGRATION_WRITE=1`. Keep `increment`, `rewrite`, and `bfg`
+out of this run. The adaptation rejects those unvalidated entry points.
+
+The numeric creation stream combines issues and PRs. Actual returned destination
+IDs and numbers determine mappings. Source number gaps consume no placeholders.
+Issue and PR titles remap bare and qualified references to those actual numbers.
+Unmapped title references retain the source repository qualifier. Original
+titles remain in the source snapshot, archive, and per-object ledger.
+GitHub rejects edits to titles longer than 256 characters. For source issue
+5776, the destination title is shortened and both complete titles, original and
+remapped, are retained in its description. This exception is audited explicitly.
+PRs use isolated source-commit refs, preserve their diffs, and are closed without
+merging. Source PRs 8280, 8863, and 8884 have no recreatable diff and become
+attributed archival issues. Original merged state remains explicit provenance.
+GitHub cannot natively reproduce original users, timestamps, approvals, checks,
+or event identities. The archive retains those available source values.
+GitHub caps a PR file list at 3,000 entries. The archive retains complete Git
+name/status history for capped diffs and checks every available API path against
+it. PR 4767 deletes 17,280 files while GitHub reports zero changed files; audits
+retain that discrepancy and verify the source and destination file entries.
+
+PR 9076 is deferred throughout historical creation, comments, updates, and ref
+cleanup. Its complete raw record and unresolved references form the final live
+PR handoff. Create exactly one open, non-draft destination PR against `main`
+only after migration leaves 2 through 8 are complete. Leave both source and
+destination PRs unmerged and open, and leave destination auto-merge disabled.
+
+`state.json` is atomically saved and paired with the append-only `state.jsonl`
+ledger. A host/PID lock admits one destination writer. Before a creation request,
+the tool saves its intent and stable provenance marker. Resume reconciles a
+possible remote success before retrying. Failed writes never count as migrated.
+If a host name changes, inspect the old worker's PID and start time before
+retiring its lock; do not weaken the lock or overwrite it while a worker lives.
+
+The research archive has one JSON record per source issue or PR. `index.json`
+supports both number directions. `links.json` supports incoming and outgoing
+queries by source URL. `coverage.json` records available history and exceptions.
+`deferred-live-pr.json` supplies the PR 9076 handoff. `SHA256SUMS` covers every
+archive file. Preserve the original Git mirror independently of synthetic refs.
+
+## Configuration and canonical identity
+
+`inventoryConfiguration` reads settings without reading secret values.
+`restoreConfiguration` consumes its reviewed plan. It verifies the history
+archive's exact audited manifest, completed ref cleanup, and closed completed
+leaves 4 and 5 before writing settings. It reads every changed setting back and
+enables Actions as its final mutation. A rerun reconciles prior successful
+writes and rejects unexpected owner edits.
+
+The personal repository retains required GitHub Actions checks. Its main-branch
+rules require an up-to-date branch and squash merges. Organization merge queues,
+team identities, inherited organization administrators, and optional organization
+runner labels do not transfer to a personal account. No numeric organization
+bypass identity is copied. The disabled review ruleset remains disabled.
+
+The destination description and original planning labels are retained. Secret
+scanning and push protection remain enabled. Empty Projects, Discussions, Pages,
+wiki, secrets, environments, webhooks, deploy keys, and self-hosted runner
+inventories require no placeholder resources. The mapped source Chief issue
+7687 becomes `LARCH_MIGRATION_CHIEF` for the repository-scoped governance workflow.
+
+After Actions restoration, use a separate canonical-identity PR to verify every
+required job and the protected squash merge path. Its changes point installation,
+upgrade, release, provenance checks, and command defaults at `zhupanov/larch`.
+Enable the corrected governance workflow after that code merges. Issue and PR
+operations use direct `gh` or API calls, as requested by the repository owner.
+
+## Releases and final validation
+
+The selected policy copies only the latest upstream release as an attributed
+baseline, then publishes a new destination-built release. `createReleases`
+reconciles by tag, creates a draft, verifies all three asset digests and bytes,
+publishes immutable, verifies the release attestation, and explicitly selects
+Latest. A rerun preserves any later Latest. Copied artifacts retain upstream
+build provenance; they do not gain destination build attestations.
+
+Production baseline import requires completed configuration and canonical
+identity leaves, plus a verified credential preflight for leaf 7. Leaf 7's final
+release, installation, upgrade, and storage tests complete after the real release.
+Use larch's checked-in release procedure for versioning, draft validation,
+immutable publication, attestations, and stable-pin promotion. Create and merge
+its PR directly with `gh`; never use an admin merge bypass.
+
+Capture a fresh read-only source watermark before cutover. Compare it with the
+immutable original snapshot and reconcile every real change through the mapping.
+Source-generated cross-reference events are recorded as such. Source archive,
+rename, deletion, or other source mutations require separate authorization.
+
+Run clean installation, upgrade, contributor, maintainer, and recovery checks.
+After leaves 2 through 8 are verified complete, refresh PR 9076 and recreate its
+current work and attributed discussion last. Append its mapping, references,
+normal CI result, and open-state proof to the final private archive and parity
+report. Close the umbrella only after that final verification.
+
+## Rehearsal and tests
+
+The isolated rehearsal is `zhupanov/larch-migration-rehearsal-20260928` with an
+explicit ten-record selection. It checks long bodies, intervening number
+consumption, interruption after remote success, comments and reviews, reference
+repair, closed unmerged PR diffs after ref cleanup, immutable release publication,
+the capped 17,280-file PR diff, the long-title API limit, and idempotence. Rehearsal completion markers are
+separate from production ones.
+Production replay, history completion, and release import each require their
+verified rehearsal report.
+
+```sh
+node --test migrationReplay.test.js migrationReferences.test.js \
+  migrationSafety.test.js historySupplement.test.js releaseMigration.test.js \
+  repositoryConfiguration.test.js historyCompletion.test.js historyFiles.test.js
+```
+
+Keep the rehearsal and reports as evidence. A successful test or checkpoint
+does not by itself complete a migration leaf; remote readback and the leaf's
+acceptance criteria are required.
